  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following Boolean expressions is not a tautology?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>By applying&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Since, the operation disjunction is commutative, hence, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now, applying the distributive law i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>Also, we know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;represents tautology.</p><p>Thus, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a tautology.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Again, using the same definitions, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is also a tautology.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is also a tautology.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Which is not a tautology.</p>"
  }
